/parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing granules for supporting a surfactant thereon which comprises a step in which granules having on the surface thereof a coating film containing a water-soluble ingredient are treated so as to have a coating film deficiency; and a process for producing detergent particles which comprises the step of mixing a surfactant composition with the granules obtained by the above process, under such conditions that the surfactant composition is in a liquid state. By the former process, surfactant-supporting granules having improved supporting ability can be obtained without lowering the detergency. Use of these granules can give detergent particles having excellent detergency.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de fabrication de granules servant de support à un surfactant, ledit procédé consistant à traiter les granules pourvues à leur surface d'un film d'enrobage contenant un ingrédient hydrosoluble de manière à ce qu'il y ait carence de film d'enrobage; et un procédé pour produire des particules détergentes qui consiste à mélanger une composition surfactante avec les granules obtenues par le processus ci-décrit, dans des conditions assurant l'état liquide de la composition surfactante. Le premier procédé permet d'obtenir des granules de support de surfactant possédant des capacités de support améliorées, et ce sans affecter les capacités détergentes. L'utilisation de ces granules peut conférer aux particules détergentes des capacités détergentes exceptionnelles.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>